[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=Calibrate touchscreen
Comment=Recalibrate the touchscreen (4-point tap)
Exec=/usr/bin/pikalibrate
Icon=pikalibrate
Terminal=false
Categories=Settings;
X-Piko-Settings-Group=Display
X-Piko-NoDesktop=true
# Categories was System, which put this in the panel menu's "System Tools"
# folder. Settings moves it to "Desktop Preferences" alongside Set
# Wallpaper -- and is what makes piko-settings list it at all, since that
# is the one word it selects on. Recalibrating the panel is a setting, not
# a system tool; the only thing lost is the old folder placement.
#
# See mb-wallpaper-picker.desktop for what the two X-Piko lines do and
# which program reads each.
